.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MAKE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm make
.Nd maintain program dependencies
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar makefile
.Op Fl nsk
.Op Fl j1
.Op Ar target ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads a makefile, updates the named targets (or the first target when none are named),
and runs recipe lines whose prerequisites are newer.
.Pp
The supported language is a bounded POSIX subset:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It variable assignment
Recursive
.Pq Ql = ,
immediate
.Pq Ql := ,
conditional
.Pq Ql ?= ,
and append
.Pq Ql += .
.It rules
Explicit rules, pattern rules with
.Ql % ,
suffix rules such as
.Ql .c.o ,
and
.Ql .PHONY .
.It automatic variables
.Ql $@ ,
.Ql $< ,
.Ql $^
and
.Ql $? .
.It include
.Ql include Ar file
and
.Ql -include Ar file .
.El
.Pp
GNU make functions such as
.Ql $(wildcard ...)
and
.Ql $(shell ...)
are not implemented.
Parallel jobs other than
.Fl j1
are an explicit unsupported error.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar makefile
Read
.Ar makefile
instead of
.Pa makefile
or
.Pa Makefile .
.It Fl n
Print recipes without running them.
.It Fl s
Do not echo recipes.
.It Fl k
Continue with other goals after a failure.
.It Fl j1
Accept one job; larger values are rejected.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a failed recipe or missing target, 2 for usage or a malformed makefile.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1
.Sh STANDARDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It POSIX.1-2024
The default goal, explicit/pattern/suffix rules, variable expansion, automatic variables,
.Ql .PHONY ,
includes and the listed options follow POSIX make.
GNU functions and parallel jobs are
documented deviations.
.El
